# Snapshots

To switch: `snap <tag>`

---

## v1-menubar-basics

**Menubar usage app (SwiftPM)**

Claude Usage menubar app built as a Swift package: logo icon, popover with session/weekly limits, first-run consent prompt, launch at login, claude.ai sign-in window. Limitations: the claude.ai sign-in and usage endpoint were not verified end to end; no settings window, notifications, forecast or widgets.

## v2-pre-clausage

**Claude Usage before the Clausage rebrand**

Mac menubar app (popover, settings, accounts, notifications, Claude Code tab, Sparkle) plus the iOS app and widgets with the in-app claude.ai sign-in and cookie data path. Feasibility research and the Clausage design handoff are committed. Limitations: the old blue/accent styling, no plan badge, product breakdown, usage credits or weekly history; the large widget's day chart still uses fixture data.

## v3-clausage-brand

**Clausage brand and new usage sections (iOS + macOS)**

Bricolage type and Paper/Ink/Sand palette across both apps; plan badge, Limiting now chip, weekly product split, running-total chart (each app records its own history), usage credits (iPhone), Claude Code contributors pane (Mac), branded widgets, popover, menu bar and Settings. Limitations: App Icon alternates and the privacy-policy link aren't built; some Mac control tints and the iPhone pull-to-refresh were only verified offscreen/in the simulator.

## v4-pre-rename

**Last version with the claude-usage identifiers**

Clausage-branded Mac and iOS apps still built as `Claude Usage.app` with bundle IDs `com.postfl.claude-usage*`, App Group `group.com.postfl.claude-usage`, the `ClaudeUsage` Xcode project and the Sparkle feed at updates.postfl.com/claude-usage. About links point to clausage.ai; `site/` has plain placeholder pages. Limitations: the clausage.ai pages are not uploaded yet.
